-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.
--
-- turtle-agent ca6fb6d (dev after PR #404): `plan-export --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --floor-aware --approach-hops
-- --mmaps <the server's mmaps> --rev ca6fb6d --stamp 20261104160000`. Round 3: the 20 plans still skipped in round 2
-- (zulfarrak stays out, its owner gap open), zul_gurub (walk 34; Arlokk's gong is the kind `open` row, entry 180526),
-- ruins_of_ahnqiraj (walk 30 and the Buru leg regen), and the round-1 plans whose turtle-agent source changed since
-- (naxxramas, ragefire_chasm, wailing_caverns). dire_maul_north and sunken_temple are left out: their regenerated rows
-- fail a TortoiseBots guard (tests/plans-export/MANIFEST.md, round 3). The boss seed rows stay in the migrations that
-- introduced them (a plan-only export writes none).

-- blackfathom_deeps: map 48, 7 legs, 443 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'blackfathom_deeps';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'blackfathom_deeps';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'blackfathom_deeps';

